      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "10cm — Phonecert",
      "content": "Connecting two actions or states. The simplest way to link ideas.\n\nPhonecert (폰서트) is a pun combining 'phone' and 'concert' — the entire premise is a private show performed just for one person over a phone call. The narrator sets it up like an actual concert, with instructions to the listener (get comfortable, keep your battery charged, stay on the line) before performing an intimate, slightly nervous set of songs meant only for them.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-고**, which means \"and / and then.\" We'll see how 10cm uses it in \"Phonecert.\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **꿈** — dream\n- **사랑** — love\n- **웃고 울다** — to laugh and cry\n- **사랑하고 싶다** — to want to love\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
